/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -9 & -1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260116} :answer-field/id #uuid "30e051d5-7b61-53d4-982a-e57239cc0e2b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262211}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "553e355c-3ed5-592a-b9a8-9897676499b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-129124" :question/problem "What is the augmented matrix for the following system of linear equations?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2y &=5-x \\\\ 5x-9y+1 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that the variables are ordered $x,y$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=5 \\\\ 5x-9y &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix  is the coefficient matrix augmented with the column that represents the right-hand sides of the equations: \n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -9 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338976 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16e9c5d7-63ce-5359-983d-17894b881c44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336247} {:answer/id #uuid "9a3ff646-483b-5d53-9784-f1957608dcab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337433} {:answer/id #uuid "d9f0bf30-c2fd-52a1-8cc4-73b48203b9d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 175921